# P0 (v3.99.4, codex ambiguity review): line-ending policy is a REPOSITORY invariant, not a
# developer setting. A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true converted admin.html and the
# suite to CRLF, and smoke's LF-sensitive source lifts ("MAG_BASKET=null;\n  {") then crashed
# the gate mid-run — a line-ending reason, reported before any behavior was evaluated.
# text=auto keeps git's binary detection; eol=lf pins every text file's CHECKOUT to LF on
# every platform, which overrides autocrlf. test/smoke.mjs normalizes its own reads too
# (readSrc), so the suite survives even a checkout that predates this file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries, stated explicitly rather than trusted to detection (the PWA icon is the one
# binary this repo currently tracks).
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
